WEBVTT

00:45.003 --> 00:48.006
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

01:01.979 --> 01:03.605
REPUBLIC OF KOREA ARMY

01:03.689 --> 01:04.856
Born in 2004.

01:04.940 --> 01:06.358
BEST TRAINEE
PRIVATE KANG SEONG-JAE

01:06.441 --> 01:07.693
Wait a second.

01:08.026 --> 01:09.319
"The Best Trainee"?

01:09.778 --> 01:10.779
Is that right?

01:11.530 --> 01:12.531
Well, look at that.

01:12.614 --> 01:15.200
We finally got an ace, huh?

01:15.284 --> 01:16.994
Private Kang Seong-jae. Thank you.

01:17.077 --> 01:18.078
Well.

01:18.161 --> 01:21.164
You've got a good voice
and you're good-looking too.

01:21.540 --> 01:22.833
Back in school, you must've...

01:23.125 --> 01:25.210
- Wait, a cat!
- Huh? What?

01:25.294 --> 01:26.545
What was that?

01:26.628 --> 01:28.922
Hey! What if you scratch up

01:29.006 --> 01:30.382
our new recruit?

01:30.465 --> 01:32.509
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Drive carefully.

01:32.593 --> 01:33.594
Be gentle.

01:34.636 --> 01:35.637
Right?

01:35.762 --> 01:37.055
Good grief.

01:38.724 --> 01:39.850
Gosh.

01:40.183 --> 01:41.935
The Best Trainee.

01:51.612 --> 01:53.238
Looking back, my life has always been

01:53.322 --> 01:54.781
a fierce battle.

01:59.661 --> 02:03.040
The villains would attack
at any time and any place

02:03.832 --> 02:06.460
and I was often overwhelmed

02:06.543 --> 02:08.712
by the sheer number of enemies.

02:12.799 --> 02:14.426
But who am I?

02:14.885 --> 02:16.762
A strong warrior of the Republic of Korea

02:16.845 --> 02:18.055
and its strong army!

02:18.138 --> 02:19.598
This war-like life...

02:20.432 --> 02:22.684
has finally made me
into the ultimate warrior...

02:23.435 --> 02:24.645
Private Kang Seong-jae!

02:30.233 --> 02:31.234
Hey.

02:31.318 --> 02:32.861
What do you make of this situation?

02:33.278 --> 02:35.197
This seems very wrong, sir.

02:35.280 --> 02:36.323
Right?

02:36.406 --> 02:37.908
It's not just because
I'm an old fart, is it?

02:37.991 --> 02:39.326
No, not at all, sir.

02:39.868 --> 02:42.037
Kids these days sleep so soundly

02:42.120 --> 02:43.872
without a care in the world.

02:48.835 --> 02:50.045
EPISODE 1

03:20.409 --> 03:22.994
GANGLIM

03:26.623 --> 03:27.624
All right.

03:28.208 --> 03:29.876
This is your home now.

03:29.960 --> 03:30.961
Got it?

03:31.044 --> 03:32.838
Fourth Company, First Battalion.

03:32.921 --> 03:34.339
60th Regiment, 29th Division.

03:34.423 --> 03:35.882
Ganglim Post.

03:37.134 --> 03:38.427
The air is amazing, isn't it?

03:39.010 --> 03:40.929
We've even had guys
cure their eczema here.

03:43.473 --> 03:46.143
Well, since you're the Best Trainee,
so I'm not worried...

03:46.393 --> 03:48.019
But still, military life

03:48.103 --> 03:49.813
with people from all over...

03:50.856 --> 03:51.857
Hey!

03:51.940 --> 03:52.941
Snap out of it.

03:53.024 --> 03:54.443
If you do that again

03:54.568 --> 03:56.486
I'll reach my limit.

03:57.362 --> 03:58.363
Yes, I understand.

03:58.447 --> 03:59.448
Let's go.

03:59.656 --> 04:03.493
Welcome to Ganglim Post.

04:11.543 --> 04:12.836
Salute! Welcome back, sir!

04:12.919 --> 04:14.045
Hey, Tak!

04:14.671 --> 04:15.672
So.

04:15.922 --> 04:17.132
Are you happy
to finally have a subordinate?

04:18.675 --> 04:19.968
I'll have to put him through a test

04:20.051 --> 04:21.344
and size him up first, sir.

04:21.428 --> 04:22.429
Hey, you jerk!

04:22.596 --> 04:23.597
Come on.

04:23.680 --> 04:24.681
At boot camp

04:24.765 --> 04:27.100
he was the Best Trainee. A real ace.

04:27.184 --> 04:28.226
What happened at boot camp

04:28.310 --> 04:30.020
doesn't mean anything out here, sir.

04:30.103 --> 04:31.730
Darn, this punk. You're already...

04:31.980 --> 04:33.106
You're already bossing a junior.

04:33.190 --> 04:34.608
Hey, put that down and come here.

04:35.400 --> 04:36.401
Yes, sir.

04:38.820 --> 04:40.197
The following individual

04:40.655 --> 04:43.992
. shown dedication and spirit
of service to his country...

04:44.075 --> 04:45.410
Man, this is good.

04:45.911 --> 04:47.788
Best Trainee, huh? The very best.

04:48.330 --> 04:49.581
The Best Trainee has arrived.

04:50.832 --> 04:51.833
PSYCHOLOGICAL EVALUATION

04:51.917 --> 04:53.502
FAMILY BACKGROUND?
SINGLE MOTHER

04:53.585 --> 04:55.337
Who's on the duty roster today?

04:55.420 --> 04:57.339
IS YOUR FAMILY HARMONIOUS?

04:57.422 --> 04:58.423
AVERAGE

04:58.507 --> 04:59.549
It's not out yet.

04:59.633 --> 05:02.761
FAMILY'S MONTHLY INCOME?
LESS THAN 1.8 MILLION WON

05:04.262 --> 05:05.263
Hey, Best Trainee.

05:05.847 --> 05:07.140
Private Kang Seong-jae.

05:07.224 --> 05:08.433
No need to lie.

05:08.517 --> 05:10.268
Be honest, write down every detail.

05:10.352 --> 05:12.938
Even how many pairs of underwear.

05:13.146 --> 05:14.147
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

05:14.356 --> 05:15.357
Sit down.

05:18.151 --> 05:20.111
- Hey, Tak.
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

05:20.445 --> 05:23.073
- Did you put out the makgeolli?
- Yes, sir. I put it in the mess.

05:23.490 --> 05:24.533
Anything to report?

05:24.616 --> 05:26.076
No, sir. Nothing.

05:29.704 --> 05:35.418
FELT LOSS OR DEPRESSION RECENTLY?
YES

05:43.969 --> 05:45.053
Welcome, Private.

05:46.263 --> 05:47.264
Hero.

05:47.347 --> 05:49.099
Private Kang Seong-jae!

05:53.270 --> 05:54.312
What are you doing?

05:55.897 --> 05:57.858
Didn't you just call me, sir?

06:12.205 --> 06:13.373
- Master Sergeant.
- Yeah?

06:15.083 --> 06:16.167
Is it out yet?

06:16.251 --> 06:17.294
Well, about that, sir.

06:18.295 --> 06:19.296
He's...

06:19.379 --> 06:20.630
S-Class, sir.

06:23.216 --> 06:25.176
S-Class? Beyond A-Class?

06:25.260 --> 06:27.095
- S-Class?
- That's a good thing, right?

06:27.178 --> 06:28.513
EXTREMELY HIGH RISK: S

06:28.597 --> 06:29.931
DEPRESSIVE SYMPTOMS
VERY HIGH

06:30.015 --> 06:31.016
GAMING ADDICTION
VERY HIGH

06:35.145 --> 06:36.146
Salute!

06:37.230 --> 06:38.231
Hey.

06:39.357 --> 06:42.402
I heard the battalion sent an ace,
so I came to check him out.

06:42.485 --> 06:43.486
Is this him?

06:43.570 --> 06:45.155
He's got that fire in his eyes.

06:45.238 --> 06:46.656
What ace?

06:47.157 --> 06:48.158
He's S-Class.

06:49.117 --> 06:52.579
What? There must've been some mix-up.

06:52.662 --> 06:53.955
Damn it. It's not the first time

06:54.039 --> 06:56.041
those jerks sent us their rejects.

06:57.792 --> 06:58.793
Hey.

06:59.085 --> 07:00.420
Private Kang Seong-jae.

07:00.503 --> 07:01.588
To the Room of Truth.

07:02.589 --> 07:03.924
Yes... to the Room of Truth.

07:07.010 --> 07:10.138
PERSONNEL RECORD CARD

07:10.221 --> 07:12.390
KANG SEONG-JAE

07:16.770 --> 07:17.979
What does your mother do?

07:18.104 --> 07:19.940
- She runs a food truck.
- A food truck?

07:21.483 --> 07:22.484
Oh, a street stall.

07:23.985 --> 07:25.028
It's not a stall.

07:25.111 --> 07:26.905
She has an official permit
from the city...

07:26.988 --> 07:28.907
Hey, it's the same thing.

07:29.199 --> 07:31.576
You little punk,
are you playing word games with me?

07:34.788 --> 07:35.789
What's this?

07:38.166 --> 07:39.376
FATHER, KANG YONG-IL
DIED TWO MONTHS PRIOR TO ENLISTMENT

07:39.459 --> 07:40.460
Your father...

07:40.794 --> 07:42.253
passed away recently.

07:45.173 --> 07:47.550
Yes, sir. He passed away two months ago.

07:47.634 --> 07:48.635
Goodness.

07:48.760 --> 07:50.011
That must've been hard on you.

07:51.805 --> 07:53.848
It was all so sudden.

07:56.601 --> 07:59.020
But I'm doing much better now.

07:59.771 --> 08:00.772
Jeez.

08:01.564 --> 08:03.566
What's all this about
being the "Best Trainee"?

08:04.150 --> 08:05.860
More like top priority high-risk soldier.

08:06.194 --> 08:07.195
Hey.

08:08.947 --> 08:10.323
Keep this pinned to your chest

08:10.407 --> 08:12.158
until I say so.

08:12.325 --> 08:13.326
Got it?

08:16.204 --> 08:18.915
When someone talks to you, you answer.

08:18.999 --> 08:21.501
- Yes, sir.
- Goodness, you're frustrating.

08:21.584 --> 08:23.670
- Hey, Tak!
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik!

08:23.753 --> 08:25.422
Take him to greet the Outpost Commander.

08:26.381 --> 08:27.507
Tell her

08:27.590 --> 08:30.385
that a tragic hero you can't watch
without crying has arrived.

08:34.222 --> 08:35.515
OUTPOST COMMANDER
FIRST LIEUTENANT CHO YE-RIN

08:36.558 --> 08:38.852
Outpost Commander, may I enter?

08:39.102 --> 08:40.103
Come in.

08:44.482 --> 08:46.192
Salute!

08:46.276 --> 08:48.153
I brought the new recruit, Commander.

08:48.236 --> 08:49.279
All right. Let me see him.

08:54.576 --> 08:55.660
Salute!

08:55.785 --> 08:56.786
Salute!

08:57.787 --> 08:59.205
Private Kang Seong-jae.

08:59.289 --> 09:02.709
On August 18, 2025, I was ordered to
report here...

09:04.044 --> 09:06.629
Kang Seong-jae has been registered.

09:06.713 --> 09:07.714
Report...

09:08.715 --> 09:09.966
Ordered...

09:10.800 --> 09:11.801
Here...

09:13.428 --> 09:15.764
KANG SEONG-JAE,
ORDINARY SOLDIER, AGE 22

09:22.062 --> 09:23.313
COMMEMORATING THE 70TH ANNIVERSARY
OF THE ROK ARMY

09:23.396 --> 09:24.814
Where are you looking?

09:28.359 --> 09:30.278
I'm sorry, I must have
seen something wrong.

09:30.361 --> 09:31.696
I don't know what's up with him.

09:31.780 --> 09:33.573
He says he sees and hears things.

09:34.991 --> 09:36.826
Everyone seems fine on the outside

09:36.910 --> 09:38.495
but they start seeing things
once they enlist.

09:39.913 --> 09:41.706
Well, okay.

09:41.956 --> 09:43.792
It's a hard environment to adjust to

09:43.875 --> 09:45.043
so I can understand.

09:45.293 --> 09:46.669
But if...

09:46.753 --> 09:48.880
if you feel like it's too difficult
to handle

09:48.963 --> 09:51.508
you must come to me before you think
of doing anything rash.

09:52.175 --> 09:53.885
No, ma'am. I'm really okay.

09:53.968 --> 09:56.054
No, you don't look okay.
That's why I'm saying it.

09:57.263 --> 09:58.848
- Mun-ik.
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

09:58.932 --> 10:00.225
- Has he eaten?
- Not yet, ma'am.

10:00.475 --> 10:01.684
Get him some food first.

10:01.768 --> 10:03.103
Yes, ma'am.

10:03.186 --> 10:05.146
LEFTOVER FOOD SIGNAL
BAD

10:11.694 --> 10:13.029
COOK SOLDIER'S PLEDGE
WITH DUTY AND DEVOTION

10:13.113 --> 10:14.447
I WILL COOK TO BOOST
MY COMRADES' HEALTH AND STRENGTH

10:32.507 --> 10:34.634
TAKE ONLY WHAT YOU CAN EAT!

10:50.024 --> 10:51.151
What is this supposed to be today?

10:51.234 --> 10:52.485
Braised potatoes.

10:52.735 --> 10:54.487
Do you think I'm asking
because I don't know what it is?

10:55.071 --> 10:56.823
I mean, is this a potato?
Or was it one at some point?

10:56.906 --> 10:58.825
It looks like it's been
chewed up and spat out.

10:58.992 --> 10:59.993
What?

11:00.076 --> 11:01.077
I mean...

11:01.494 --> 11:02.829
I'm asking for anything fancy.

11:02.912 --> 11:05.290
Please just make something
that's at least edible.

11:10.920 --> 11:12.130
I think this is supposed to be...

11:12.672 --> 11:14.048
like mashed potatoes, isn't it?

11:14.340 --> 11:15.466
It's American-style.

11:16.092 --> 11:17.093
Next.

11:21.222 --> 11:22.682
Hey, Yoon Dong-hyun is the cook.

11:22.765 --> 11:24.225
How is he getting bigger?

11:24.309 --> 11:26.728
Didn't you see him lifting pork
as weights the other day?

11:28.730 --> 11:29.898
And for his meals

11:29.981 --> 11:32.942
I hear he only picks out the tofu
and chicken breast to eat.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.195
It seems he's a kitchen soldier
not to cook

11:35.278 --> 11:37.655
but to get his protein.

11:39.657 --> 11:40.658
This tastes like shit.

11:42.285 --> 11:46.414
VIGILANCE IS OUR MISSION

11:47.916 --> 11:50.335
Pretty soon, you'll be crying
that you want to go home.

11:51.127 --> 11:53.254
- Wanna go home? Should I call a cab?
- No, sir.

11:53.338 --> 11:56.424
You think any of us were born
here in Ganglim?

11:56.507 --> 11:59.844
You better brace yourself
before we go into the mess hall.

12:00.136 --> 12:02.847
Something straight out of hell
is waiting for you in there.

12:02.931 --> 12:05.225
VIGILANCE THOROUGH AND MISSION PERFECT

12:10.772 --> 12:12.106
Sirs.

12:14.943 --> 12:16.319
Hey, the new guy's here.

12:16.861 --> 12:18.363
Squad 3, Squad 1.

12:18.446 --> 12:19.572
Isn't he ours this time?

12:21.741 --> 12:23.117
KANG SEONG-JAE ROK ARMY

12:23.201 --> 12:25.495
Man, we're screwed again.

12:25.578 --> 12:27.080
Not another smiley face.

12:27.163 --> 12:29.832
Is this a dumping ground?
Why do we only get guys like him?

12:31.000 --> 12:32.043
Tell me about it.

12:34.587 --> 12:37.382
- Hey, TMI.
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

12:37.715 --> 12:38.716
Is that the new recruit?

12:38.800 --> 12:39.801
Yes, sir.

12:44.055 --> 12:45.515
Thank... thank you for the food.

12:46.349 --> 12:47.433
Thanks for the food.

12:50.561 --> 12:52.188
Hey.

12:54.524 --> 12:56.526
- Hey.
- Let's go.

12:59.612 --> 13:01.155
Damn, they smelled fresh meat.

13:01.698 --> 13:02.699
Go on.

13:14.002 --> 13:15.128
How old is our little newbie?

13:15.253 --> 13:17.255
- Private Kang...
- Keep it down.

13:18.214 --> 13:19.465
Sorry, sir.

13:19.549 --> 13:21.676
- This guy is...
- Was I talking to you?

13:24.387 --> 13:25.805
I'm... sorry, sir.

13:26.097 --> 13:27.932
Private Kang Seong-jae.
I'm twenty-two years old.

13:29.017 --> 13:30.601
You're older than you look.

13:30.977 --> 13:32.520
Did you go to some fancy university?

13:32.854 --> 13:35.815
- No, sir. I worked before enlisting.
- Oh, working.

13:35.898 --> 13:37.442
And what amazing job was that?

13:39.235 --> 13:41.654
- Just... a bit of this and that.
- Oh, "this and that".

13:41.738 --> 13:42.989
So, "it's none of your business," huh?

13:43.573 --> 13:44.991
No, sir. That's not it.

13:45.074 --> 13:46.659
Gosh, just from a few words

13:46.743 --> 13:48.411
I can tell you're a special one.

13:48.494 --> 13:51.080
I swear they handpick
these landmines just for us.

13:55.501 --> 13:57.295
Damn, he's totally green. Hey, TMI.

13:57.378 --> 13:58.504
Private First Class TMI... I mean...

13:59.505 --> 14:01.049
- Tak Mun-ik.
- Not living up to the nickname, huh?

14:01.924 --> 14:04.010
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Does a top school make you better?

14:05.261 --> 14:07.722
No, sir. I'll make sure
he's properly trained.

14:10.266 --> 14:11.642
Did you enlist not knowing
how tough army life is?

14:13.311 --> 14:14.937
You think it's over after boot camp

14:15.021 --> 14:16.606
but you see how much time is left

14:16.689 --> 14:17.899
and have no clue how to survive, right?

14:18.107 --> 14:19.692
What can you do? If you can't avoid it...

14:19.776 --> 14:21.235
- You have to enjoy it.
- That's right.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.281
Now, when I press this badge

14:25.365 --> 14:27.200
you have to be happy, no matter what.

14:27.700 --> 14:29.369
- Got it?
- Yes, sir.

14:30.370 --> 14:31.371
Well?

14:33.206 --> 14:34.457
Private Kang Seong-jae.

14:34.540 --> 14:37.085
Guess you're not too thrilled
about meeting such great seniors.

14:37.168 --> 14:38.378
Is that the best laugh you've got?

14:44.467 --> 14:45.927
Private Kang Seong-jae.

14:47.387 --> 14:50.515
- P-Dragon.
- Private Pyo Ji-yong.

14:54.560 --> 14:56.187
This is so much fun.

14:56.479 --> 14:57.772
I'm so excited.

15:05.655 --> 15:06.697
What are you doing?

15:09.033 --> 15:10.576
He looked so tense

15:10.660 --> 15:11.953
so we were just messing with him.

15:12.453 --> 15:14.539
If you're bored, go peel some onions.

15:16.374 --> 15:18.042
- TMI.
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

15:18.126 --> 15:20.086
Take the new recruit over there
and eat quietly.

15:20.378 --> 15:21.379
Understood.

15:30.930 --> 15:32.765
He's the top dog of our outpost

15:32.849 --> 15:34.016
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

15:34.100 --> 15:35.935
You can tell he's someone
not to mess with, right?

15:36.394 --> 15:37.603
Physically, I mean.

15:37.687 --> 15:39.480
No, sir. He looks like a nice guy.

15:39.564 --> 15:40.982
He is a nice person.

15:41.774 --> 15:42.859
As long as he's not the cook.

15:42.942 --> 15:44.152
Sorry, what was that?

15:44.235 --> 15:46.279
Control your expression while you eat.

15:47.238 --> 15:48.656
He's watching.

16:08.092 --> 16:09.218
Hey, hey, hey!

16:09.844 --> 16:11.345
Get a grip, will you?

16:11.596 --> 16:12.722
Sorry.

16:13.222 --> 16:14.223
So, how is it?

16:14.682 --> 16:16.893
Makes boot camp slop
seem gourmet, doesn't it?

16:17.435 --> 16:19.937
What can you do?
Even though today's is a bit salty

16:20.021 --> 16:21.397
this is one of the edible batches.

17:02.855 --> 17:04.106
What is this?

17:08.528 --> 17:09.529
What?

17:11.697 --> 17:15.284
Help me!

17:28.839 --> 17:29.966
Help me!

17:32.134 --> 17:33.177
What are you doing?

17:43.145 --> 17:44.730
- It's too salty...
- "Salty?"

17:44.897 --> 17:46.732
Look at this punk complaining.

17:47.233 --> 17:49.527
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
did you hear that?

17:50.069 --> 17:53.531
The rookie says the food you made
tastes bad,

17:53.614 --> 17:54.824
and dissing you right to your face.

17:55.157 --> 17:56.909
What do you think about that, sir?

17:58.661 --> 18:01.205
If you don't like it,
you can cook it yourself!

18:02.039 --> 18:03.499
You can cook it yourself!

18:05.459 --> 18:06.627
Oh, no, sir.

18:08.796 --> 18:10.423
I'm sorry.

18:20.474 --> 18:21.851
CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT: HWANG SEOK-HO

18:21.934 --> 18:23.561
AWARD CERTIFICATE,
CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION

18:27.481 --> 18:30.610
These beans are from a friend of mine
who grows them in Kenya.

18:32.278 --> 18:33.279
It's...

18:36.991 --> 18:38.242
The aroma is just different.

18:38.326 --> 18:40.411
You'll be surprised when you try it.

18:40.494 --> 18:41.579
Well...

18:41.662 --> 18:43.664
I really only drink instant coffee.

18:46.083 --> 18:47.418
A lot of soldiers enlist

18:47.501 --> 18:50.129
with this vague sense of dread.

18:50.421 --> 18:51.631
Seong-jae.

18:51.714 --> 18:52.715
You're a little scared, aren't you?

18:53.132 --> 18:55.217
Private Kang Seong-jae. No, sir.

18:56.427 --> 18:58.471
Well, the military shown in the media

18:58.554 --> 18:59.680
is often quite violent

18:59.764 --> 19:00.890
so I can see why you might think that.

19:01.057 --> 19:02.183
But the truth is...

19:02.266 --> 19:04.685
that's just unbelievable
in this day and age, right?

19:05.061 --> 19:06.896
Now a Sergeant's salary is one million won

19:06.979 --> 19:08.981
it's not the old days of brute force.

19:09.440 --> 19:10.900
Things have changed completely.

19:12.693 --> 19:13.861
Isn't that right, Master Sergeant?

19:15.363 --> 19:17.198
Yes, that's right. In any case...

19:17.823 --> 19:19.283
these days, in the army

19:19.367 --> 19:21.118
soldiers study for entrance exams

19:21.202 --> 19:22.870
and even pass the civil service exam.

19:26.123 --> 19:27.583
Some people

19:27.667 --> 19:31.545
can't perceive the unique aroma
and taste of coffee.

19:31.629 --> 19:32.838
and will only say it's bitter, won't they?

19:33.089 --> 19:35.383
It's not that I dislike good coffee.
I just prefer the instant mix.

19:35.466 --> 19:37.885
But if you concentrate a little more...

19:38.386 --> 19:39.887
sometimes you can smell a floral scent

19:40.304 --> 19:43.891
and sometimes, you can even smell
the earth that grew the fruit.

19:44.433 --> 19:46.185
Seong-jae, as your Company Commander

19:46.644 --> 19:49.021
I think coffee is a lot like the military.

19:49.480 --> 19:50.940
Just a thought, you know?

19:51.440 --> 19:54.318
You can have a mediocre time here, or...

19:54.777 --> 19:57.113
you could have a major
turning point in your life.

19:59.949 --> 20:00.950
Here.

20:02.118 --> 20:03.452
Thank you, sir.

20:12.837 --> 20:15.214
So your mother runs a food truck?

20:16.799 --> 20:17.800
Yes, sir.

20:17.883 --> 20:21.137
There's something so romantic
about street food.

20:21.637 --> 20:23.055
So, what kind of food

20:23.139 --> 20:25.307
does your mom make?

20:25.808 --> 20:29.270
American West-style Chinese food?

20:29.353 --> 20:31.897
Or Mexican tacos and burritos?

20:33.357 --> 20:34.900
She sells tteokbokki.

20:35.985 --> 20:37.445
Oh, and fried snacks and sundae as well.

20:39.697 --> 20:40.698
So, Tteok-Sun-Twi?

20:43.284 --> 20:44.285
Let's make him a cook.

20:46.287 --> 20:47.288
What?

20:48.497 --> 20:49.498
Hero.

20:49.582 --> 20:50.958
Isn't there an open spot?

20:51.375 --> 20:54.462
The Chef's Path tutorial has begun.

20:54.545 --> 20:55.629
Make him a cook?

20:55.713 --> 20:57.798
Sir, isn't that a bit much?

20:59.175 --> 21:00.968
- Why is that?
- What do you mean, "Why"?

21:01.051 --> 21:02.219
Hero.

21:02.303 --> 21:05.264
The fate of this world is in your hands.

21:06.640 --> 21:07.892
From this moment on

21:07.975 --> 21:10.686
your journey to become The Legendary Chef

21:10.770 --> 21:12.062
begins.

21:12.146 --> 21:14.106
That place is full of incidents
and accidents

21:14.190 --> 21:16.859
If we send a kid like him there
for no good reason...

21:16.942 --> 21:19.028
High risk, high return, Master Sergeant.

21:19.361 --> 21:21.864
I, Hwang Seok-ho,
am a man who enjoys taking risks.

21:22.406 --> 21:25.534
Who knows?
This could make our Kang Seong-jae

21:25.618 --> 21:27.995
a great chef, every bit
as good as his mother.

21:30.790 --> 21:33.042
Hey, what's the best dish you can make?

21:34.627 --> 21:37.254
- I can make ramyun, sir.
- Ramyun.

21:37.338 --> 21:39.632
- Making good ramyun isn't easy.
- Ramyun...

21:39.715 --> 21:42.510
Eyeballing the water level...
it's not easy without a natural gift.

21:42.593 --> 21:44.845
- Ramyun!
- It's absolutely not easy.

21:45.346 --> 21:46.347
Okay.

21:48.891 --> 21:50.309
You're going to be a kitchen soldier.

21:50.392 --> 21:51.560
Thank you for your service.

21:53.270 --> 21:54.897
Private Kang Seong-jae!

21:54.980 --> 21:56.482
Sir! Yes, I can!

21:56.565 --> 21:57.775
I will do my best, sir!

21:59.443 --> 22:00.486
Ramyun...

22:16.710 --> 22:17.878
ROK ARMY

22:17.962 --> 22:19.255
KANG SEONG-JAE

22:20.840 --> 22:22.091
Kang Seong-jae.

22:22.174 --> 22:23.551
Private Kang Seong-jae!

22:25.135 --> 22:26.387
What did you do before enlisting?

22:27.179 --> 22:29.306
I delivered water and worked nights
at a convenience store.

22:29.390 --> 22:30.808
What's First In, First Out?

22:31.475 --> 22:33.102
It's ordering items by expiry date

22:33.185 --> 22:34.520
so the older ones get sold first.

22:34.895 --> 22:36.605
Oh, good.

22:36.981 --> 22:38.148
In that case...

22:38.232 --> 22:40.901
organize all these provisions
using First In, First Out.

22:43.571 --> 22:45.239
You mean everything here, sir?

22:49.535 --> 22:51.495
Was I unclear?

22:51.579 --> 22:52.872
No, sir. I'll get right on it.

22:52.955 --> 22:53.956
That's right.

22:54.498 --> 22:55.499
Get started.

22:55.708 --> 22:57.209
- I'm heading out.
- Yes, sir.

22:57.710 --> 22:58.794
Salute!

22:58.878 --> 22:59.879
Good luck.

23:00.838 --> 23:02.006
Yes, sir.

23:05.551 --> 23:08.554
Hey, are you trying to pick a fight
with me right now?

23:08.762 --> 23:10.389
You sent a high-risk soldier

23:10.472 --> 23:12.892
to the outpost with live ammunition?

23:13.100 --> 23:16.020
It's not the first time
we've had one of those guys around.

23:16.103 --> 23:18.147
How are we supposed to screen out
those who are struggling?

23:18.230 --> 23:19.231
Besides.

23:19.315 --> 23:22.693
Managing the soldiers is your job,
isn't it, Master Sergeant?

23:23.319 --> 23:25.571
Don't try to pin the responsibility
for personnel decisions on us.

23:25.654 --> 23:26.655
What are you talking about?

23:26.739 --> 23:30.034
He's depressed and addicted to games.

23:30.117 --> 23:32.828
The kid just got back
from mourning his father, and what?

23:32.912 --> 23:33.913
He's an ace?

23:33.996 --> 23:35.247
You call that an "ace"?

23:35.331 --> 23:37.124
What are you gonna do
if this blows up in our faces again?

23:37.207 --> 23:39.585
Anyway, you pull something
like this one more time

23:39.668 --> 23:41.754
my patience will have its limits.

23:41.837 --> 23:43.505
Listen, Master Sergeant.

23:43.881 --> 23:46.425
Things are already tense at battalion HQ.

23:46.508 --> 23:47.551
Aren't you going too far?

23:47.635 --> 23:49.637
That's your problem, not mine.

23:49.720 --> 23:51.221
Got it?

23:53.015 --> 23:55.434
Damn, what is with this guy?

24:00.648 --> 24:01.649
Oh, hello.

24:03.484 --> 24:05.736
I guess the Personnel Officer
isn't in yet.

24:05.819 --> 24:07.112
Oh, right.

24:07.196 --> 24:09.365
He's swamped with all the
personnel transfers.

24:10.991 --> 24:12.201
Congratulations in advance.

24:12.493 --> 24:14.078
I heard you're getting promoted.

24:14.161 --> 24:16.038
Oh, thank you.

24:16.747 --> 24:18.374
It's just a change in rank insignia

24:18.457 --> 24:19.583
but I already feel the weight.

24:19.667 --> 24:21.085
That must be a lot of pressure.

24:21.168 --> 24:22.336
It comes with the territory.

24:23.379 --> 24:25.339
Things have been too chaotic for a while

24:25.422 --> 24:27.925
so I'll try to handle things
quietly and efficiently.

24:28.801 --> 24:30.594
By the way, is something the matter?

24:31.178 --> 24:32.680
Your voice was booming

24:32.763 --> 24:34.181
which is unlike you, Master Sergeant Heo.

24:36.892 --> 24:37.893
It's...

24:37.977 --> 24:40.688
- the Administration &amp; Supply NCO
- Oh.

24:41.313 --> 24:43.107
- Master Sergeant Park Jae-young?
- Yes.

24:43.190 --> 24:46.443
He's raising hell,
saying the new recruit is unfit.

24:46.527 --> 24:49.571
Goodness, that guy's at it again, huh?

24:50.280 --> 24:53.075
I don't get why everyone
in the 4th Company is so quick to blame.

24:53.534 --> 24:55.160
Seeing you so upset, Master Sergeant Heo

24:55.452 --> 24:57.121
how can I just stand by and do nothing?

24:57.663 --> 24:58.664
Where are you going?

25:00.416 --> 25:01.834
I can't just let this go.

25:02.376 --> 25:03.502
We're not their punching bag.

25:07.798 --> 25:09.216
How am I supposed to organize all this?

25:13.262 --> 25:14.263
Jeez.

25:14.763 --> 25:16.765
How long has this been here?

25:22.855 --> 25:25.816
You've gone from an ordinary hero
to a Kitchen Assistant.

25:34.241 --> 25:36.243
USER INFORMATION

25:41.206 --> 25:42.207
USER INFORMATION

25:43.584 --> 25:48.547
USER INFORMATION

25:50.591 --> 25:53.594
You are currently
Kitchen Assistant, Level One.

25:53.677 --> 25:54.678
GANGLIM OUTPOST
173CM/59KG AB RH(+)

25:54.762 --> 25:56.346
NAME: KANG SEONG-JAE
AGE: 22

25:56.847 --> 25:58.140
INFORMATION

25:58.223 --> 25:59.266
What is all this?

26:00.142 --> 26:02.227
You can use the basic skills

26:02.311 --> 26:04.646
Organizing Ingredients &amp; Chef's Eye.

26:04.730 --> 26:05.856
SKILLS

26:06.440 --> 26:08.150
Well begun is half done.

26:08.233 --> 26:10.402
Your first quest will now begin.

26:10.486 --> 26:12.529
USE A SKILL: ORGANIZE THE STOREROOM
REWARD: 100 EXPERIENCE POINTS

26:27.711 --> 26:29.171
Damn it.

26:29.254 --> 26:31.590
I told him to come inside
when it's time to eat.

26:32.424 --> 26:33.425
INSPECTION

26:37.554 --> 26:38.555
Salute.

26:41.767 --> 26:43.143
There's still grease here.

26:43.227 --> 26:45.062
Are you even cleaning or not?

26:46.814 --> 26:48.690
Who told you to leave
wet rags out like this?

26:48.774 --> 26:50.984
If this causes a norovirus outbreak
and food poisoning

26:51.068 --> 26:52.236
will you take responsibility?

26:52.694 --> 26:54.196
You need to dry these out
completely in the sun.

26:54.530 --> 26:55.572
Yes, sir.

26:55.948 --> 26:58.575
This is why the higher-ups
are losing sleep over Ganglim.

26:58.826 --> 27:01.745
I know guard post life is tough,
but isn't this going too far?

27:03.038 --> 27:04.331
Did you report it to the Master Sergeant?

27:04.414 --> 27:06.542
- That I'm here?
- Master Sergeant

27:06.625 --> 27:08.460
went for supplies.

27:09.378 --> 27:10.712
He's not just hiding out
and slacking off somewhere, is he?

27:11.922 --> 27:15.259
Does he still knock back
bowls of makgeolli on duty?

27:16.635 --> 27:18.011
And what's the Outpost Commander doing?

27:21.181 --> 27:22.182
Right.

27:29.481 --> 27:31.692
- Salute!
- When was this fridge last cleaned?

27:31.984 --> 27:33.152
About that, sir.

27:33.402 --> 27:35.279
I'm the only one managing
the mess hall, so...

27:35.404 --> 27:36.905
Refrigerator condition, unacceptable.

27:39.116 --> 27:42.202
Sir, what brings you here
without any notice?

27:42.452 --> 27:45.414
It's a surprise inspection.
Should I have sent an announcement?

27:46.915 --> 27:48.333
If the kitchen looks like this

27:48.417 --> 27:49.793
I can only imagine the storeroom.

27:52.129 --> 27:54.006
- What do we do?
- What is it now?

27:54.089 --> 27:55.174
The new recruit

27:55.257 --> 27:56.842
- is in the storeroom.
- What?

28:00.721 --> 28:01.722
Salute!

28:02.848 --> 28:04.933
- A Private?
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

28:06.101 --> 28:07.394
Damn.

28:07.477 --> 28:10.063
This unit has gone completely insane, huh?

28:11.440 --> 28:12.900
A brand new recruit is organizing?

28:12.983 --> 28:15.152
What could he possibly know?

28:16.361 --> 28:17.696
You all are unbelievable.

28:28.165 --> 28:30.459
From the inventory,
organized with military precision...

28:31.752 --> 28:35.005
to the bags of rice, perfectly spaced
from the wall to prevent dampness...

28:36.215 --> 28:37.216
It's perfect.

28:40.052 --> 28:41.929
You didn't happen to get
the inspection checklist...

28:42.596 --> 28:43.680
ahead of time, did you?

28:44.348 --> 28:45.557
Of course not, sir.

28:45.641 --> 28:47.309
I only just learned you were here.

28:48.477 --> 28:50.812
Why leave a Private by himself?
What if something had happened?

28:51.813 --> 28:54.775
And then you'd be first to complain
about the soldier's welfare.

28:55.567 --> 28:57.277
What's that supposed to mean, sir?

29:01.448 --> 29:02.741
What I'm trying to say is...

29:03.325 --> 29:06.286
managing your soldiers is also
part of managing the kitchen.

29:06.578 --> 29:08.163
Pay attention.

29:08.247 --> 29:09.748
Do I have to spell it out for you?

29:12.125 --> 29:13.126
In any case...

29:13.210 --> 29:14.211
this is all a mess.

29:14.878 --> 29:15.879
A complete mess!

29:37.109 --> 29:38.360
From now on

29:38.443 --> 29:39.861
let's try to get along.

29:39.945 --> 29:41.113
We're one family in this battalion.

29:42.614 --> 29:44.324
Oh, "family."

29:45.284 --> 29:47.577
What kind of family
just barges in unannounced?

29:49.454 --> 29:52.416
You still haven't figured out
why you were sent here.

29:53.875 --> 29:56.044
- Of course I know.
- And you still act this way?

29:59.381 --> 30:00.674
Just do your job right.

30:01.258 --> 30:02.259
Ye-rin.

30:06.847 --> 30:07.848
Salute.

30:13.145 --> 30:14.146
So...

30:14.229 --> 30:16.481
what's going to happen to us?

30:16.565 --> 30:19.234
If he reports this
to the Company Commander

30:19.318 --> 30:20.527
we will lose our leave.

30:22.571 --> 30:25.073
I didn't know I had leave to lose.

30:27.576 --> 30:29.745
- Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Quest complete.

30:30.620 --> 30:32.622
You have completed
"Organizing the Storeroom."

30:32.706 --> 30:33.999
YOUR KITCHEN ASSISTANT
LEVEL HAS INCREASED

30:36.585 --> 30:38.712
Come on, get a grip, Seong-jae. Okay?

30:38.795 --> 30:40.005
ORGANIZING INGREDIENTS

30:40.088 --> 30:41.465
Get it together.

30:47.471 --> 30:48.722
What the...

30:54.478 --> 30:55.562
Something just...

31:11.370 --> 31:12.829
Why is this so light?

31:25.926 --> 31:27.260
LEVEL UP AND GROW STRONGER
WITH A VARIETY OF SKILLS

31:27.344 --> 31:31.431
Level up and grow stronger...

31:31.932 --> 31:33.975
with a variety of skills.

31:36.061 --> 31:37.604
Levels? Skills?

31:39.314 --> 31:40.732
This isn't a video game.

31:40.816 --> 31:43.777
Do you want to use The Chef's Eye?

31:44.403 --> 31:45.654
The Chef's Eye.

31:48.865 --> 31:50.742
While focused

31:51.243 --> 31:52.911
close your eyes.

31:54.246 --> 31:55.664
Take a deep breath

31:55.747 --> 31:56.832
and open your eyes.

31:57.374 --> 31:59.751
The Chef's Eye

31:59.835 --> 32:01.253
will automatically activate.

32:15.267 --> 32:17.018
SEAWEED, RAMEN, NOODLES

32:17.102 --> 32:19.146
COOKING OIL, FLOUR, CANNED TUNA, RICE,
SEASONING, SWEET CORN

32:20.439 --> 32:22.107
SPAGHETTI SAUCE, SALT, SUGAR,
KETCHUP, TONKATSU SAUCE, SOY SAUCE...

32:23.108 --> 32:24.568
APPLE CIDER VINEGAR

32:24.651 --> 32:27.696
Apple Cider Vinegar.
Origin, Osan Factory, Gyeonggi.

32:31.741 --> 32:33.452
Wait, that thing from earlier...

32:37.080 --> 32:38.623
This is past its expiration date.

32:38.707 --> 32:40.333
It needs to be discarded.

32:44.296 --> 32:45.505
It really works?

32:45.589 --> 32:46.631
After making meals daily,
I have afternoon duties.

32:46.715 --> 32:47.966
Quest complete.

32:48.049 --> 32:50.552
- When am I supposed to do that?
- Gained 100 experience points.

32:50.635 --> 32:53.054
- I work the night shift with no sleep.
- Level up.

33:03.190 --> 33:04.191
What are you doing?

33:09.613 --> 33:11.865
I thought I saw a bug flying around.

33:13.909 --> 33:15.118
Well, of course.

33:15.452 --> 33:17.454
This place hasn't been cleaned properly.

33:18.455 --> 33:19.456
Seong-jae?

33:20.415 --> 33:21.917
Private Kang Seong-jae.

33:22.000 --> 33:23.210
Can I talk to you for a minute?

33:23.460 --> 33:24.461
Yes, ma'am.

33:28.256 --> 33:29.674
Get going, you idiot.

33:31.468 --> 33:33.345
Run, you idiot! Hurry!

33:42.437 --> 33:46.107
MY GROWTH ENVIRONMENT
PERSONNEL RECORD CARD

33:48.860 --> 33:49.861
All right.

33:49.945 --> 33:51.780
I heard what happened, more or less.

33:52.280 --> 33:55.951
The Company Commander tends to be
impulsive and just acts on his moods

33:56.535 --> 33:58.328
so I bet you're confused about

33:58.411 --> 33:59.538
how you ended up as a Cook.

34:00.247 --> 34:01.248
Right?

34:01.414 --> 34:02.415
Yes, ma'am.

34:03.333 --> 34:04.334
That's the army for you.

34:05.001 --> 34:06.920
- Just do your best.
- View a new recipe.

34:07.003 --> 34:08.004
Besides, you were
cleaning up well earlier.

34:15.762 --> 34:17.472
But what have you been
staring at this whole time?

34:18.682 --> 34:20.600
Are you possessed by some spirit

34:20.684 --> 34:23.353
claiming you're going to meet
General MacArthur or something?

34:30.527 --> 34:32.028
I go to church.

34:38.451 --> 34:40.704
That's a relief, then.

34:42.330 --> 34:44.749
We've had guys
say things like that before.

34:45.041 --> 34:46.084
I was just checking.

34:47.127 --> 34:49.421
Does that happen often?

34:49.713 --> 34:53.216
Well, not often,
but we get guys like that sometimes.

34:53.675 --> 34:55.885
You know, suddenly seeing things

34:56.219 --> 34:57.596
or hearing voices.

34:57.679 --> 35:00.557
VIEW NEW RECIPE

35:01.433 --> 35:02.434
What?

35:02.517 --> 35:03.602
Why did the Support Section Chief come?

35:05.312 --> 35:06.563
According to the Outpost Commander

35:06.855 --> 35:08.857
he did a surprise inspection

35:08.940 --> 35:10.692
and tore through the kitchen and storage.

35:11.276 --> 35:12.277
Those sons of bitches.

35:12.360 --> 35:13.945
All because I told off
Master Sergeant Heo.

35:14.029 --> 35:15.780
They come crawling back here
being all petty

35:16.072 --> 35:18.033
and start trouble in the mess hall
for no reason.

35:18.116 --> 35:20.952
Is the Company Commander
going to lose his shit again?

35:21.494 --> 35:22.746
Of course he is.

35:22.829 --> 35:25.040
You think a guy who loves raising hell
is going to pass this up?

35:25.582 --> 35:28.376
He's already jealous his peer made Major

35:28.460 --> 35:30.086
so his bitching has tripled.

35:30.629 --> 35:32.422
Now he's complaining
I don't know anything about coffee.

35:32.797 --> 35:34.924
If he studied as much as he complains
about coffee, he'd be a Major by now.

35:36.009 --> 35:37.844
But about that new recruit.

35:38.637 --> 35:40.472
What? Did that kid
already get into trouble?

35:40.889 --> 35:43.600
No. He looks fine, handsome even, but...

35:43.892 --> 35:45.935
Sometimes his gaze is unfocused

35:46.186 --> 35:47.354
and I get a bad vibe from him.

35:47.437 --> 35:49.105
He was acting weird
during the inspection, too.

35:49.189 --> 35:51.858
He blurted out his rank and name
and started looking all around.

35:51.941 --> 35:53.401
You saw it too, didn't you,
Master Sergeant?

35:53.485 --> 35:56.029
You don't think he's going
to cause any trouble, do you?

35:57.072 --> 35:58.782
Come on. It's always the same guys

35:58.865 --> 36:00.408
who act crazy or play sick at first.

36:00.492 --> 36:01.743
We see it all the time.

36:02.285 --> 36:04.079
But that kid, Kang Seong-jae...

36:04.162 --> 36:06.414
is like a landmine.

36:06.498 --> 36:09.250
He's a ticking time bomb.

36:09.417 --> 36:10.960
Hey, does the paperwork ever lie?

36:11.044 --> 36:12.295
No, it has not, sir.

36:12.462 --> 36:16.216
Why would the Company Commander
put that guy in the kitchen?

36:17.217 --> 36:18.218
Hey.

36:18.843 --> 36:20.345
Make it clear to Yoon Dong-hyun.

36:20.428 --> 36:22.764
Kang Seong-jae must not hold a knife.

36:36.486 --> 36:37.529
Here, use this.

36:38.196 --> 36:39.864
Oh, thank you.

36:40.699 --> 36:42.659
I thought you were all skin and bones

36:42.867 --> 36:45.328
but you've actually got
some real muscle on you.

36:45.995 --> 36:48.164
But you know you need more than
just the hardware, right?

36:48.790 --> 36:50.792
When it comes to cooking,
what's really important

36:50.875 --> 36:53.795
is the software that figures out

36:53.878 --> 36:55.088
how the ingredients work together.

36:55.588 --> 36:56.589
Is that right?

36:57.215 --> 36:59.968
You know the biggest mistake
rookies like you make when cooking?

37:00.051 --> 37:02.846
They get excited and start throwing
everything in together.

37:02.971 --> 37:06.307
They end up with slop that
even the army cats won't touch.

37:09.227 --> 37:10.228
Man.

37:10.729 --> 37:13.064
You'll figure it out
as your service goes on.

37:20.822 --> 37:21.948
Use it and bring it back.

37:22.031 --> 37:23.366
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

37:29.873 --> 37:30.874
Tell me.

37:32.751 --> 37:34.043
I checked him out.

37:34.127 --> 37:36.212
He's got depression, a gaming addiction...

37:36.337 --> 37:38.214
He's the complete
"high-risk soldier" package.

37:38.298 --> 37:40.341
Then why bring him to the kitchen?

37:40.425 --> 37:42.469
Are they out to ruin a career? Damn it.

37:42.719 --> 37:44.846
The Company Commander thinks the kitchen's
an easy place to dump him.

37:44.929 --> 37:46.264
So watch yourself.

37:46.890 --> 37:48.475
Don't get tangled up with him,
with your discharge so close.

37:52.395 --> 37:54.647
Exactly one hundred days until I'm out.

37:55.940 --> 37:57.484
Just let me make it until then, please.

38:03.198 --> 38:05.241
- Recipe acquired.
- What the...

38:05.325 --> 38:07.869
ACQUIRED RECIPE

38:07.952 --> 38:11.539
BEEF SEAWEED SOUP

38:12.582 --> 38:14.459
Check your new recipe.

38:27.430 --> 38:30.058
Why's he acting like that by himself?

38:31.226 --> 38:32.435
It's so creepy.

38:35.438 --> 38:36.981
I will turn off the lights.

38:38.900 --> 38:41.486
- Have a good night.
- Good night.

39:00.088 --> 39:02.173
Saving system.

39:02.924 --> 39:04.926
Do not shut down.

39:07.470 --> 39:09.138
Let me get some sleep.

39:10.265 --> 39:11.474
I can't sleep.

39:11.558 --> 39:13.852
It's too bright.

39:17.605 --> 39:19.232
Oh, come on.

39:23.862 --> 39:25.113
Just a hundred days.

39:27.448 --> 39:28.783
Just a hundred more days.

39:38.501 --> 39:42.672
GANGLIM

39:46.009 --> 39:47.010
Kang Seong-jae.

39:47.886 --> 39:49.470
Hey, Kang Seong-jae.

39:51.347 --> 39:52.765
Hey, Kang Seong-jae, get up!

39:53.766 --> 39:55.018
Go away.

39:55.435 --> 39:56.936
Is this bastard crazy?

39:57.520 --> 39:59.355
Hey, get up.

39:59.439 --> 40:02.734
A quest... Seriously, what do I do?

40:04.027 --> 40:06.279
- Hey!
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

40:06.571 --> 40:07.572
You punk.

40:07.864 --> 40:09.157
Do you think you're still at home?

40:09.449 --> 40:10.742
Get changed and get out here.

40:12.076 --> 40:13.077
Yes, sir.

40:15.997 --> 40:18.833
Goodness gracious.

40:41.230 --> 40:43.358
BREAKFAST
BEEF SEAWEED SOUP

40:44.525 --> 40:47.570
The Beef Seaweed Soup recipe
is now available.

40:50.114 --> 40:52.241
Make that floor gleam.

40:52.325 --> 40:54.661
You never know
when inspectors might drop in again.

40:54.869 --> 40:55.870
Yes, sir.

40:57.080 --> 40:59.707
I told you, didn't I?
This thing about making food...

40:59.791 --> 41:01.501
It looks like you can just wing it

41:01.584 --> 41:03.503
but... you see... this...

41:03.586 --> 41:04.712
You punk.

41:05.505 --> 41:06.506
Just go buff the floor.

41:06.756 --> 41:07.757
Yes, sir.

41:13.513 --> 41:20.144
AVAILABLE RECIPE
BEEF SEAWEED SOUP

41:24.023 --> 41:27.735
IRONCLAD COASTAL DEFENSE.
UNITED THROUGH CAMARADERIE

41:53.094 --> 41:58.474
SOUP SOY SAUCE, DARK SOY SAUCE

42:12.363 --> 42:13.489
Hey, rookie.

42:13.573 --> 42:14.574
Private First Class Lee Jeong-seok.

42:14.657 --> 42:15.783
What's today's menu?

42:15.867 --> 42:17.452
Today's breakfast is seaweed soup

42:17.535 --> 42:19.662
sausage stir-fry and seasoned seaweed.

42:19.746 --> 42:22.373
Is it Corporal Kim Gwan-cheol's
birthday today?

42:22.457 --> 42:23.541
The menu's killer, sir.

42:23.624 --> 42:26.252
Killer? More like it's so disgusting
it'll make you sick.

42:26.335 --> 42:29.338
Come on, sir. This is a foolproof menu.

42:29.422 --> 42:31.174
But our chef always manages

42:31.257 --> 42:33.134
to fail beyond all expectations.

42:33.718 --> 42:34.719
All right.

42:34.802 --> 42:36.262
Let's survive today!

42:36.387 --> 42:37.430
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

42:41.476 --> 42:43.936
This isn't a birthday feast.
It's a fatal meal.

42:44.020 --> 42:46.022
I really don't get it, sir.

42:46.564 --> 42:47.899
Is making this that...

42:50.860 --> 42:51.861
hard?

42:51.944 --> 42:54.489
What the hell is this seaweed soup?

42:54.572 --> 42:55.740
The soup is pitch-black.

42:55.823 --> 42:57.992
It looks like it would kill you, sir.

42:58.117 --> 42:59.368
Come on, no way.

43:00.495 --> 43:01.788
It's not like
it's going to actually kill us.

43:32.610 --> 43:34.737
Corporal Kim Gwan-cheol!

43:35.780 --> 43:37.907
Corporal Kim Gwan-cheol!

43:38.741 --> 43:40.326
Snap out of it!

43:47.583 --> 43:49.335
My bad. Let's move out!

43:56.801 --> 43:57.844
Are you okay?

43:58.928 --> 43:59.929
Is everyone okay?

44:00.012 --> 44:01.139
Corporal Kim.

44:01.222 --> 44:02.932
I want to live, sir!

44:03.474 --> 44:04.475
Are you okay?

44:05.810 --> 44:07.145
Once this battle is over...

44:07.353 --> 44:10.273
I'm gonna go on leave
and tell my girlfriend that I love her.

44:11.023 --> 44:12.316
That's a classic war movie trope.

44:12.400 --> 44:13.776
You look at her picture and die.

44:14.068 --> 44:15.069
You son of a...

44:21.409 --> 44:23.619
- Ji-yong!
- Ji-yong!

44:23.703 --> 44:25.037
Ji-yong!

44:27.415 --> 44:29.167
Just how bad could they make it?

44:30.710 --> 44:33.588
Taste it!

44:39.552 --> 44:40.761
No!

44:41.846 --> 44:44.640
Taste it!

44:50.897 --> 44:53.399
- No!
- Mun-ik... Mun-ik!

45:03.075 --> 45:04.076
I'm alive, sir.

45:12.376 --> 45:16.339
- Mun-ik!
- Mun-ik!

45:20.635 --> 45:22.970
- You bastards!
- Eat it!

45:23.054 --> 45:24.138
Eat it all!

45:30.061 --> 45:32.772
Help me!

45:44.242 --> 45:45.993
This is so gross!

45:56.545 --> 45:58.256
I really can't stand this!

45:59.507 --> 46:02.760
Is cooking really that hard for you?

46:03.177 --> 46:04.512
Go on, try this seaweed soup.

46:04.595 --> 46:06.597
I've never tasted anything like it.

46:07.056 --> 46:08.057
Eat.

46:09.100 --> 46:11.102
You can't be doing this
with the people's tax money.

46:12.019 --> 46:13.604
Do you even taste it before you serve it?

46:13.854 --> 46:14.939
I said, eat.

46:16.983 --> 46:18.526
Stop wasting a spot on a guy like that

46:18.609 --> 46:20.945
and just ask for a decent cook.

46:21.028 --> 46:22.280
If you want to complain so much

46:22.363 --> 46:23.864
you go tell them yourself.

46:23.948 --> 46:26.659
Tell them to pick some
decent guys for a change.

46:28.119 --> 46:30.037
It's not like I asked for the moon.

46:30.246 --> 46:32.748
Is it really that hard for a cook
to cook well?

46:32.915 --> 46:33.916
Damn it!

46:42.633 --> 46:44.135
That punk with seniority thinks

46:44.218 --> 46:46.721
he can treat a senior Sergeant like dirt.

46:46.804 --> 46:47.805
I oughta just...

46:53.477 --> 46:55.730
Looks like everyone's here.
Close up in five.

46:55.813 --> 46:56.814
I'm leaving.

46:56.897 --> 46:58.441
Don't look for me. I'm on edge.

47:08.576 --> 47:11.620
It would be nice
if the rising sun lasted forever...

47:12.663 --> 47:14.081
but after the night passes...

47:14.749 --> 47:16.292
a new sun is bound to rise.

47:18.085 --> 47:19.962
The unit was in the dark for a while...

47:20.671 --> 47:22.548
but it seems the sun
is starting to shine again.

47:23.716 --> 47:25.134
Try to forget about that incident...

47:25.426 --> 47:26.719
and think only of good things.

47:27.470 --> 47:28.721
What do you mean, sir?

47:29.305 --> 47:32.266
You still have so much more to do.

47:32.350 --> 47:33.642
It's just such a shame.

47:34.602 --> 47:37.897
How could he get so greedy
over some cash to end up like that?

47:38.189 --> 47:40.024
Life is unpredictable, isn't it?

47:41.150 --> 47:43.778
He was the most promising cadet
in the academy's history...

47:44.111 --> 47:45.696
and ended up like that overnight.

47:46.447 --> 47:48.324
Who would have ever known?

47:48.908 --> 47:49.909
Jeez.

47:52.119 --> 47:53.454
Anyway, 4th Company Commander.

47:54.121 --> 47:55.873
About the Ganglim Outpost meals.

47:55.956 --> 47:57.500
There were a lot of problems.

47:57.583 --> 47:58.793
Aren't you keeping an eye on things?

48:00.044 --> 48:01.670
What issues are you referring to, sir?

48:01.754 --> 48:03.381
Don't tell me you're not aware.

48:03.964 --> 48:05.216
Based on my personal inspection

48:05.758 --> 48:07.468
the kitchen was in a complete mess.

48:09.512 --> 48:11.847
So it was a surprise inspection.

48:11.931 --> 48:14.225
Honestly, you people...

48:14.308 --> 48:16.352
An army's power comes from its food.

48:16.435 --> 48:19.063
Soldiers' entire day revolves around
wondering what's on the menu

48:19.146 --> 48:20.439
their moods rising and falling with it.

48:20.523 --> 48:22.441
And you can't even manage
to get that right.

48:23.734 --> 48:25.569
I'll take immediate corrective action.

48:25.736 --> 48:26.821
Instead of just that...

48:27.154 --> 48:30.366
If you go from the Baemgol fork,
you'll see Ganglim Outpost, right?

48:30.783 --> 48:31.784
That's right.

48:31.867 --> 48:33.494
It should only take
about an hour to get there.

48:33.577 --> 48:34.829
Why not head over for breakfast?

48:34.912 --> 48:36.414
We can also check on the mess hall.

48:46.090 --> 48:47.299
Be careful on your way down, sir.

48:48.300 --> 48:50.344
Emergency! The Battalion Commander
is on his way to the outpost.

48:50.428 --> 48:51.887
He wants to inspect today's breakfast.

48:55.307 --> 48:58.144
I just finished my duty shift
and on my way home.

48:59.311 --> 49:00.604
Turn the car around, now!

49:03.023 --> 49:05.192
Can't I just go home for once?

49:15.786 --> 49:17.538
- Salute!
- What?

49:17.621 --> 49:19.206
Are you alone? Where's Yoon Dong-hyun?

49:19.582 --> 49:20.875
Well...

49:21.584 --> 49:22.751
He left a little while ago.

49:23.794 --> 49:26.005
Mealtime isn't over. Is he crazy?

49:26.088 --> 49:27.548
Do you not know where he went?

49:31.844 --> 49:33.804
To my beloved.

49:33.888 --> 49:36.056
Present her with a meal

49:36.140 --> 49:37.558
that would make Michelin envious.

49:37.725 --> 49:40.978
To women, a man
who can cook is more appealing

49:41.061 --> 49:43.272
than any other kind of sex appeal.

49:50.488 --> 49:51.822
Just for 99 days.

49:52.907 --> 49:54.992
He made this mess and just took off?

49:58.412 --> 50:00.080
And why is the seaweed soup so black?

50:14.512 --> 50:15.554
Hey, you!

50:16.138 --> 50:18.140
- Hey!
- I'm sorry.

50:20.142 --> 50:21.143
Forget it.

50:21.227 --> 50:22.603
What can I even expect from you?

50:23.479 --> 50:26.357
The Battalion Commander is coming,
and I can't serve this.

50:30.152 --> 50:32.071
A new quest has arrived.

50:32.863 --> 50:36.534
Cooking for the first time is so hard.

50:37.243 --> 50:39.703
Complete the seaweed soup
for the Battalion Commander.

50:40.120 --> 50:42.206
REWARD: 100 EXPERIENCE POINTS

50:43.165 --> 50:45.251
Would you like to use

50:45.751 --> 50:47.545
the acquired Beef Seaweed Soup recipe?

50:48.462 --> 50:49.797
Stop wasting a spot on a guy like that

50:49.880 --> 50:52.258
and just ask for a decent cook.

50:52.341 --> 50:55.928
Who knows?
This could make our Kang Seong-jae

50:56.011 --> 50:58.389
a great chef, every bit
as good as his mother.

51:08.315 --> 51:09.316
Outpost Commander.

51:10.234 --> 51:12.486
Well, if it's all right...

51:12.570 --> 51:15.322
may I try making the seaweed soup again?

51:17.908 --> 51:18.909
Can you cook?

51:22.037 --> 51:23.247
I'm not sure about other dishes

51:23.330 --> 51:25.165
but I think I can make seaweed soup.

51:27.001 --> 51:28.002
You think so?

51:28.836 --> 51:30.337
It's gotta be better than this, right?

51:31.922 --> 51:32.923
All right.

51:35.593 --> 51:36.677
Here, watch this.

51:36.760 --> 51:37.845
I'm going to go change.

51:38.637 --> 51:40.556
Yoon Dong-hyun, that punk.
Just wait till I get my hands on him.

51:40.639 --> 51:42.224
USE ACQUIRED RECIPE?
BEEF SEAWEED SOUP

51:43.684 --> 51:45.728
ADD SEAWEED, MEAT, AND STIR-FRY

51:55.237 --> 51:56.989
Loading recipe.

52:05.539 --> 52:07.041
When rehydrating dried seaweed in water

52:07.124 --> 52:09.710
be careful, as it will
expand significantly.

52:14.131 --> 52:16.967
Stir-fry the beef with sesame oil.

52:19.553 --> 52:20.638
Beef.

52:29.480 --> 52:31.106
What? Why isn't there any?

52:33.859 --> 52:35.527
We used it all this morning.

52:35.778 --> 52:38.947
But can I make seaweed soup without beef?

52:47.498 --> 52:49.208
HIDDEN ITEM
UNKNOWN ITEM

53:03.889 --> 53:05.641
Hidden item. Sea urchin roe

53:09.144 --> 53:10.145
Hero.

53:10.604 --> 53:13.357
Would you like to use
sea urchin roe instead of beef?

53:13.440 --> 53:15.401
WOULD YOU LIKE TO USE
SEA URCHIN ROE INSTEAD OF BEEF?

53:33.377 --> 53:34.837
What's he looking at?

54:04.700 --> 54:06.744
When the broth starts to boil

54:06.827 --> 54:08.245
add soup soy sauce to season.

54:32.269 --> 54:33.270
Found it.

54:33.520 --> 54:34.563
My secret weapon.

54:42.863 --> 54:45.073
By adapting the Beef Seaweed Soup recipe

54:45.365 --> 54:47.701
you have completed
Sea Urchin Seaweed Soup.

54:47.785 --> 54:49.536
SEA URCHIN SEAWEED SOUP.
ADDITION OF GRADE A SEA URCHIN ROE

54:50.537 --> 54:51.622
Creativity score.

54:51.705 --> 54:53.540
An additional half star awarded.

54:53.624 --> 54:55.375
SEA URCHIN SEAWEED SOUP.
ADDITION OF GRADE A SEA URCHIN ROE

54:59.254 --> 55:00.297
Is this really mess hall food?

55:00.380 --> 55:01.590
Do we get sea urchin roe on base?

55:02.841 --> 55:03.842
Yes, sir.

55:03.967 --> 55:04.968
We do.

55:05.427 --> 55:06.970
Well, sometimes

55:07.054 --> 55:08.347
through the local fishermen

55:08.430 --> 55:10.724
we get some very precious sea urchin roe

55:11.266 --> 55:13.393
and make seaweed soup with it like this.

55:14.228 --> 55:15.938
If you use ingredients that aren't
from official military supply

55:16.021 --> 55:17.523
who takes responsibility for that?

55:18.982 --> 55:20.108
All right, now.

55:20.192 --> 55:22.903
I'm starving.
Let's eat first and talk later.

55:25.697 --> 55:28.742
- Let's eat.
- Private Kang Seong-jae! Enjoy!

55:28.826 --> 55:29.868
Enjoy your meal, sir.

55:32.120 --> 55:33.413
What's going on all of a sudden?

55:33.497 --> 55:34.915
Even the Battalion Commander is here.

55:34.998 --> 55:36.333
Mealtime isn't even over.

55:36.416 --> 55:37.751
Where have you been?

55:38.460 --> 55:39.920
I had some milk this morning

55:40.003 --> 55:42.297
and had some stomach trouble.

55:43.257 --> 55:44.258
By the way

55:44.341 --> 55:45.884
who made that?

55:46.385 --> 55:48.637
Who do you think? Kang Seong-jae made it.

55:48.971 --> 55:49.972
What?

55:52.057 --> 55:54.643
Looks like the soldiers left for me.

55:54.726 --> 55:56.478
I should be grateful.

56:25.465 --> 56:26.800
- Battalion Commander.
- Battalion Commander.

57:03.921 --> 57:04.963
I'm so screwed.

57:30.530 --> 57:32.991
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

57:33.909 --> 57:35.702
Do you have any idea
what you've just done?

57:35.953 --> 57:37.788
Nurse, hurry!

57:38.580 --> 57:40.832
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Where are you trying to send him?

57:41.625 --> 57:45.253
Complete the Class Change Quest
within 72 hours.

57:45.420 --> 57:47.172
I want to stay on as a cook.

57:47.631 --> 57:50.133
I thought the Company Commander said
to transfer to TOD.

57:51.051 --> 57:53.095
How will you change his mind?

57:53.178 --> 57:55.055
If words don't work

57:55.138 --> 57:56.682
there must be other ways, right?

57:56.765 --> 57:58.225
Why is this so refreshing?

57:59.351 --> 58:02.521
What is it you see in Kang Seong-jae?
Why are you so set on keeping him?

58:02.896 --> 58:04.815
It was an outstanding seaweed soup.

58:05.816 --> 58:08.151
Ending The Chef's Path.
